{"term":{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0001496","compactId":"SO_0001496","id":"SO:0001496","label":"telomeric_repeat","definition":{"text":"The telomeric repeat is a repeat region, part of the chromosome, which in yeast, is a G-rich terminal sequence of the form (TG(1-3))n or more precisely ((TG)(1-6)TG(2-3))n.","xrefs":["PMID:8720065"]},"comments":["The repeats are maintained by telomerase and there is generally 300 (+/-) 75 bp of TG(1-3) at a given end. Telomeric repeats function in completing chromosome replication and protecting the ends from degradation and end-to-end fusions. This term was requested 2009-10-16 by Michel Dumontier, tracker id 2880739."],"synonyms":[{"scope":"exact","value":"INSDC_qualifier:telomeric_repeat"},{"scope":"exact","value":"telomeric repeat"},{"scope":"broad","value":"INSDC_feature:repeat_region"}],"xrefs":[],"subsets":[],"altIds":[],"namespace":"sequence","isObsolete":false,"replacedBy":[],"canonicalUrl":"/browser/current_release/term/SO:0001496/","history":{"firstSeen":{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files"},"mostRecent":{"hash":"5fe48bd4b720f8b140cb0f77461798c55532c097","shortHash":"5fe48bd","date":"2018-01-26","subject":"Add INSDC mappings"},"entries":[{"hash":"5fe48bd4b720f8b140cb0f77461798c55532c097","shortHash":"5fe48bd","date":"2018-01-26","subject":"Add INSDC mappings"},{"hash":"92e3cae9f3d39e5979110bad332c5fadf7a4b3ab","shortHash":"92e3cae","date":"2016-12-05","subject":"Add renamed SO files"}]},"parents":["SO:0000657"],"children":[],"ancestors":["SO:0000657","SO:0001411","SO:0000001","SO:0000110"],"descendants":[],"relationships":[{"predicate":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/so#part_of","target":"SO:0000624"}],"graphNeighborhood":{"parents":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0000657"],"children":[],"related":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0000624"]}},"graph":{"parents":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SO_0000657","